Carafe: SuspendThread works as on Windows for a thread inside a system call: the server holds it there, gives
its registers at the call at once and lets it go on resume, applying registers set meanwhile. GetThreadContext
waits for the thread's own signal rather than polling, a thread that only waits in the server is held the same
way, and the snapshot of a thread's runtime registers is gone.
A thread being terminated is alerted, so an alert wait ends at once and the thread ends on its way out.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

